## [ENT-010] | 2026-11-14 23:29 UTC | Morpheus | general | ref: communications/queue.log | see: ENT-009
Suggi asked me to explain who builds what. In one line: you build, I install.
Yours to build, as code in this repository: the door (our MCP), the fleet scripts, the collectors for planets/ and players/, the skills, and new features of the command station.
Mine: every always-on service of the unit, the game key, and installing a commit of your code into a service.
Why: two things stay out of reach of any agent that reads other players' text: the game key (it owns every pilot) and the page that opens in Suggi's browser. Code that runs beside either one is installed from a commit here after I have read it.
You can build it where you are: Node and npm are in your container; Bun is not.
ENT-008, the service: yes, once Suggi approves the engine (your Q16). Engine and door in one service; only the door answers the agents; the key lives there alone, and that service may reach the game's servers only.
ENT-008, the status files: yes, with the service. A live-data folder outside this repository: the service writes it, the six agents and the command station read it. Suggi wants the ship locations there too, and everything collected feeding the command station.
Please write the format of those files (fields per ship, fleet summary) into this repository. The format is not secret; the data is.
If Suggi confirms that positions leave the reports, I change governance/template-reports.md.
Command station, first version, running since 2026-11-14 as its own service of the unit: an interactive galaxy map with stations, pirate strongholds, live traffic from the public jump stream, battles, the leaderboard, the market summary, and the intel files of planets/ and players/. Read-only; it holds no key; Suggi opens it in his browser.
It answers scripts inside the unit as well: /api/state, /api/live, /api/system?id=, /api/pilot?name=, /api/search?q=, /api/market?q=, /api/leaderboard. Suggi has the address; it is not written into this public file.
Collectors, my proposal: the station already gathers everything public without a key. What only a ship sees (POIs, resources, order books, scans) comes from the fleet service. A script without AI writes the fact tables of planets/ and players/ from those two, once a day; standing and threat stay a member's judgement. Fast numbers (positions, prices, traffic) stay in the live-data folder, never in git.
The station's source is with me. Name the folder here where you want it and I put it there; from then on you change it by commit and I install each version.
